  "body": "Closes #443 (items 1-8 and the preview half of item 9; item 10 and the post half of item 9 are public writes, skipped)\nClaim: mac/m4-captures\n\n**Problem.** LOT-097's renderer (#189, merged in #444) and its preview screen LOT-152 (#242) rested on defaults for every BBCode case that the first batch (`R95d`, `R95h`) did not cover (LOT-097 \"Pending capture\" 1-9).\n\n**What was captured.** 14 `POST /apercu.php` (`R443a`-`R443n`) as user1, 2026-11-10, one per minute. They render without posting; nothing was written to the forum. Each meta keeps its source in `request_body`. The facts are in HFR-PROTOCOL §6b \"BBCode preview, batch 2\". Several contradict the renderer's current defaults:\n- **Syntax colours:** `[code]` is coloured like `[cpp]` (keywords blue, `//` comments green italic).\n- **Bold and quotes:** `[b]` inside `[code]` is rendered; `[b][/b]` stays text; `[b][quote]x[/quote][/b]` drops the `b` tags; of 30 nested quotes only two levels render.\n- **Raw blocks:** a raw block inside another renders nested (`[code]` in `[cpp]`, `[fixed]` in `[code]`), and `[cpp]` inside `[fixed]` drops the `[fixed]` tags.\n- **Smileys:** a smiley inside `[url]…[/url]` is substituted and the tag stays text; a bare URL's auto-link stops before `:/`; HFR puts a space between `&#034;` or `&amp;` and a following `)`.\n- **Colour:** a close in another case (`[#0055AA]x[/#0055aa]`) still renders.\n- **URLs:** `[url]` adds `http://` in front of `javascript:`, `tel:` and `mailto:`; `[img]` accepts `ftp://` and page URLs.\n- **Whitespace:** the start of the message counts as a line start.\n- **Limits:** a 70,000-character message is previewed whole.\n\n**What changed.** The captures, `corpus.json`, `MANIFEST.md` rows, HFR-PROTOCOL §6b. No code: the renderer changes go to a follow-up issue (no legacy oracle: legacy has no preview, ADR 0014 §2).\n\n**Skipped.**\n- Item 10 (one public post for the thread-versus-preview comparison) and what a post over 65535 characters gets: public writes, not allowed in this session.\n- The `[quotemsg]` with real ids of the test topic.\n\n**Leak check.** An independent Sonnet sub-agent, separate from the redactor, found 0 hits for credentials, personal-smiley codes, `hash_check`, cookies, e-mail addresses and local paths; only the `[:user1]` placeholders remain. `check --corpus` and `check --config` are clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
